\title{ssDamageHunter: Single-Stranded DNA Damage Calling from PTA-Based Single-Cell WGS}
\description{
Identifies single-stranded DNA damage in single-cell whole-genome sequencing data. Starting from the somatic candidate set, each candidate is assigned likelihoods under three competing hypotheses -- a double-stranded somatic mutation, single-stranded damage present on only one strand, and an amplification or sequencing error -- and classified accordingly. Also provides detection-sensitivity and effective-callable-region estimation for converting counts into per-genome burdens.
